source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: With every `}}` hidden behind a backslash pair the run holds no closer at all; jiro refuses the span too, but its plain text reads one backslash of each pair where Jira renders the first pair literally and the second as a forced newline.
-- input.jira --
{{a\\}}b\\}}
-- rendered.html --
<p>{{a\\}}b<br class="atl-forced-newline" />}}</p>
-- want.md --
{{a\\}}b\\}}
-- warnings.json --
[]
